==Battleground==
*Infinite [[Croconator]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 13.33~16.67 seconds<sup>400f~500f</sup>.
*30 [[Croconator]]s spawn after 6.67 seconds<sup>200f</sup>, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.
*When the base reaches 99% HP:
**1 [[Director Kurosawah]] spawns as the boss.
**3 [[CyberFace]]s spawn, delay 26.67~30 seconds<sup>800f~900f</sup>.
**50 [[Croconator]]s spawn, delay 4~5 seconds<sup>120f~150f</sup>.
**30 [[Croconator]]s spawn, delay 2~3 seconds<sup>60f~90f</sup>.
**30 [[Croconator]]s spawn, delay 1~2 seconds<sup>30f~60f</sup>.

==Strategy==
The main threat of this stage are the three CyberFaces which spawn periodically during Croconator spam. Units with high attack rate are recommended to handle the Croconators. CyberFace can be killed by a stray [[Critical Hit|crit]] or chipped through the aforementioned quick-attacking units. Once the three threats are eliminated, the stage is effectively over.

Research [[Cossack Cat (Rare Cat)|Royal Guard Cat]] is able to shred every metal threat in this stage due to its incredibly high attack rate and immunity to CyberFace's [[Wave Attack]]. Simply spam them continuously on stage start.

If you don't have Royal Guard Cat, [[Sumo Cat (Special Cat)|Sumo Cat]] with research combos can handle the opening Croconators and net a large amount of money. Spam them off cooldown on stage start. When the CyberFace spawns, let it vaporize your Sumo stack and lure it to the base. A single crit spells the end of each, so spawn high-frequency [[:Category:Critical Hit Cats|critters]] like [[Catornado (Super Rare Cat)|Catyphoon]] and [[Aku Researcher (Rare Cat)|Aku Researcher]] during its backswing. [[Miracle Performance (Combo)|Miracle Performance]] can help with ensuring one procs. Once killed, continue spamming Sumo Cats to prevent Kurosawah from pushing into your base. Repeat this process twice more until none remain.

The cleanup phase is easy: continue to spam Sumo Cats to handle the peons and units like [[Ancient Egg: N101 (Rare Cat)|Courier Cat]] or [[Slime Cat (Rare Cat)|Jelly Dumpling Cat]] deal chip damage to Kurosawah.

